# The raster module's clang-tidy config (E3): native/.clang-tidy (cppcoreguidelines,
# bugprone, performance, modernize — every warning an error) plus this
# directory's headers, minus the checks below, each disabled for a stated reason.
#
#   cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-avoid-unchecked-container-access
#       operator[] on std::vector / std::array. The painters are the TS painters
#       ported line for line (textLayout.ts, vectorDraw.ts, …) so they stay
#       reviewable against them; their indices are loop-bounded by the container's
#       own size. ASan (the sanitizer presets) covers them at runtime.
#   modernize-use-designated-initializers
#       Pt / BPt / Gradient::Stop / Mat2D are value tuples mirroring the TS object
#       literals ({x, y}); naming every field at each site doubles the line
#       without catching anything the distinct types do not already catch.
#   bugprone-branch-clone
#       The ports keep the TS's branch structure (e.g. resolveAlign's switch has
#       cases with identical bodies) so a diff against the TS stays readable.
#   cppcoreguidelines-avoid-do-while / readability-function-cognitive-complexity
#       paintTextInBox / layoutText / layoutVerticalText are single long
#       functions in the TS; splitting them in the port would break the
#       one-to-one reading the parity work relies on.
Checks: >
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-avoid-unchecked-container-access,
  -modernize-use-designated-initializers,
  -bugprone-branch-clone,
  -readability-function-cognitive-complexity
InheritParentConfig: true
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*(native[/\\](include|libs)|raster)[/\\].*'
